Important requirements

Your program should:

Use variables appropriately.
Use arithmetic calculations.
Use at least 2–3 functions.
Use conditions to apply company policies.
Use lists where they make sense.
Handle different employee expense situations.
Produce a clear final report.
Test cases

Before considering the project complete, test your program with at least these scenarios:

Test Case 1 — Normal employee

5 travel days with expenses within the company's limits.

Test Case 2 — High expenses

5 travel days where food and hotel expenses significantly exceed the limits.

Test Case 3 — Low expenses

3 travel days where all expenses are below the maximum reimbursement limits.

Test Case 4 — Mixed expenses

7 travel days where some categories are below their limits and others exceed them.